@format 1
@id media-loading.in-audio
@title In Audio
@section Media loading
@area In Audio
@entry audio-items-add
@summary Show the Audio-specific initialization that runs only after new media entries have been added to the program Files docket.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag audio

@alias audio = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PAudioTab

[audio-items-add] Newly loaded Audio entries announced <input>
~ This starts with newly loaded Audio entries announced.
[Technical explanation]
= PListDocketAddHandle has finished inserting new docket entries and invokes PListItemsAdd with all newly added entries.
> audio-items-result

[audio-items-result] Persistent Audio carry active <decision>
~ The program checks whether Audio has saved settings that should be copied to the new entries.
[Technical explanation]
- PAudioItemsHandle returns when plan loading is active or Audio persistent mode is off; otherwise it reads the carried Audio plan for the newly loaded entries @ audio.PAudioItemsHandle(...)
? "Persistent carry applies" > audio-items-save
? "No persistent carry" > audio-items-nochange

[audio-items-save] Save carried plan for each new entry <process>
~ This step handles save carried plan for each new entry.
[Technical explanation]
- For every newly loaded entry, read any source-specific Audio plan, resolve it against the persistent carried plan, and save the resolved plan @ audio.PAudioItemsHandle(...)
> audio-items-saved

[audio-items-nochange] Loaded entries need no Audio initialization <output>
~ This path ends with loaded entries need no Audio initialization.
[Technical explanation]
= PListItemsAdd causes no Audio plan write while persistent carry does not apply.

[audio-items-saved] Loaded Audio entries initialized <output>
~ This path ends with loaded Audio entries initialized.
[Technical explanation]
= Persistent Audio state has been resolved and saved for every newly loaded media entry.
